PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — parallel disjoint-slot mesh flattening,
upstreamable to leap71/PicoGKRuntime verbatim.

Applied to vendor/PicoGKRuntime by scripts/fetch-deps.sh. Kept as a patch
because it modifies dependency source; no flag-level override exists.

1. Source/PicoGKMesh.h — adds a bulk-construction seam (BulkResize /
   aVertexData / aTriangleData / FinalizeBulk) so a caller can pre-size the
   vertex and triangle arrays and fill disjoint slots in parallel, then
   restore the bbox/memusage invariants in one step. nAddVertex/nAddTriangle
   remain the incremental path.
2. Source/PicoGKVdbVoxels.h — roAsMesh() drives openvdb's VolumeToMesh class
   directly instead of tools::volumeToMesh: the vector adapter behind that
   entry point copies primitives one element at a time on one thread, and the
   facade then re-copied points and triangles element-wise a second time
   (per-vertex bbox updates, per-triangle asserts, no reserve). Replaced by
   pool-indexed count -> prefix sum -> parallel emission into pre-sized
   disjoint slots, plus a parallel point copy + bbox reduce. Output bytes are
   identical to the serial path: same point order, same pool-order primitive
   concatenation, same winding reversal; Include() is pure per-axis min/max
   so the bbox reduction is order-independent bit-for-bit. This also makes
   emission order independent of allocation order — the property the mimalloc
   NO-GO (bench/results/webgpu-v2/SK-0.1.md) was missing.

Evidence: docs/research/picogk-runtime-performance-deficiency-audit.md
(F16 cluster), docs/research/gpu-surface-extraction-survey.md (disjoint-slot
polygon discipline), bench/results/webgpu-v2/SK-0.6.md.

Updated for flat-mode: roAsMesh() now calls enableFlatQuadOutput() and
consumes flatQuads()+leaf offsets/counts when active (see the sibling
patches/openvdb/0001-flat-quad-output.patch); the pool path remains as the
generic fallback.
